prudynt-t: pick the antiflicker freq form per platform

0002-add-t32-platform.patch rewrote attr.freq to T32-only enum names,
breaking T40/T41: their IMPISPAntiflickerAttr.freq is uint8_t and no
IMPISP_ANTIFLICKER_FREQ_* enum exists there. Dropping back to plain
numbers breaks T32 instead: T32 2.2.0 declares freq as
IMPISPAntiflickerFreq, and C++ rejects an int-to-enum assignment.
Guard the assignment by platform. The two enumerators are 50 and 60, so
the values agree either way.

diff --git a/src/isp/imp_hal.cpp b/src/isp/imp_hal.cpp
index a6733e2..f8a5d2b 100644
--- a/src/isp/imp_hal.cpp
+++ b/src/isp/imp_hal.cpp
@@ -948,8 +948,13 @@ int set_anti_flicker(int mode) {
   IMPISPAntiflickerAttr attr{};
   attr.mode = (mode == 0) ? IMPISP_ANTIFLICKER_DISABLE_MODE
                           : IMPISP_ANTIFLICKER_NORMAL_MODE;
+#if defined(PLATFORM_T32)
   attr.freq =
       (mode == 2) ? IMPISP_ANTIFLICKER_FREQ_60HZ : IMPISP_ANTIFLICKER_FREQ_50HZ;
+#else
+  /* T40/T41: freq is uint8_t, plain Hz */
+  attr.freq = (mode == 2) ? 60 : 50;
+#endif
   return IMP_ISP_Tuning_SetAntiFlickerAttr(IMPVI, &attr);
 #else
   IMPISPAntiflickerAttr attr = IMPISP_ANTIFLICKER_DISABLE;
